;BKEX3
 
%Hints-for-the-Advanced-Explorer
 
You might like to try writing SIMPL/E programs to:
 
  give more sophisticated voice control
  give robot more autonomy (to wander around lasing things)
  get the robot to go somewhere distant with a single command
  get the robot to follow you automatically
  combine voice-control of the robot and the matter transmitter
    to obviate the need for a lift
;BKRB22
%Basic-Principles-of-Robotics
 
1. The COMPUZZ robot is essentially very simple. Most of the mechanical
   movements are hydraulic servos, with the occasional stepper motor.
 
2. Robot speech is synthesised using a phoneme generator, with linear
   predictive encoding used to give some stress to the articulation.
 
3. Robot vision is quite sophisticated, and is described in chapter 6.
 
4. COMPUZZ robots have position sensors which, by detecting the cosmic
   background radiation are capable of an accuracy of a few metres.
 
5. COMPUZZ robots are strictly non-Asimovian in their behaviour. Indeed
   this is implicit in any burglar-repelling device. Be warned!
;BKRB23
 
%Voice-Control
 
When programming the ROBOT to deal with voice I/O, take note of the
following:
 
 1.  speech (via ROBOT_VOICE) takes time (1 tick)
 2.  if nothing was SAY'd, ROBOT_EAR is set to "hash"
 3.  INTERPRET can be used to powerful effect, but beware, since
       unchecked input, if interpreted, may lead to an ABEND
 4.  avoid looping without some sort of time-delay. Test the time
       before and after, and if unchanged do a WAIT 1
 5.  although COMPUZZ robots can be driven hard (multi-tasking means that
      several robot commands can be obeyed in 1 tick) this can lead to
      unpredictable effects, overloading the computer, abends etc.
;BKTR0
