;BKPM2
%Introduction
 
  SIMPL/E (Simple Interpreted Multi-Purpose Language / Extensible) is
  a language designed to run on COMPUZZ computers.
 
  This manual describes version 4.
 
%Blanks-in-SIMPL/E
 
There are a number of%required-blanks in SIMPL/E:
 
  before and after the ':' when labelling a statement
  before and after the operator in an expression
  before and after the '=' in a SET
 
 
;BKPM8
%Error-Recovery
 
When a program abends, an automatic TELL is performed. This TELL has the
form:  TELL (ERROR) nnn ppp vvv nnn
 Where nnn is the abend number (901 -999)
       ppp is the program name
       vvv is the program version
       nnn is the line number where the abend occurred
 
Thus, if a program called ERROR is running, it can PULL this information
and use it as desired (e.g. to restart the program that failed).
 
A sample ERROR program is supplied on one of the disks.
;BKPM16
.sssc
 The next page is intentionally left blank. This page is blank apart
 from this message.
;BKPM17
;BKPM20
 Error Messages
 
 The error messages (which all accompany an ABEND - there is no soft
 failure feature as yet) are self-explanatory.
;BKHE0
